// Typed holes: the machine answers instead of rejecting.
//
// An empty block is a *hole*. gandr's pipeline lowers every parseable input
// totally -- out-of-fragment or missing pieces become holes -- and the typing
// machine reports each hole as a GOAL (the type it needs you to provide)
// rather than an error. Holey items are not evaluated; the goal is the
// answer. This is the interactive workflow the typing machine is built
// around: write the shape, let the machine tell you what goes in the gaps.
{ }

// The harness checks:
//@ expect: goal
